treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbe in Boeotia. Evans 
describes the find as coming from a funerary context and frames his study as 
offering “a glimpse into the Minoan after-world,” emphasizing that the imagery 
on the ring and associated items reflects Minoan religious or afterlife 
concepts. The work provides the foundational publication for the ring’s 
identification, description, contextualization within a tomb assemblage, and 
cultural attribution within the broader Minoan–Mycenaean world, and includes 
detailed descriptions and plates of the ring’s iconography and associated 
objects.",
